{
    "background_story": "Alonzo was a charismatic 17th-century Italian musician who traveled from town to town, playing his lively tunes on the lute. One day, while performing in a small village, he stumbled upon a mysterious and ancient ritual. The villagers, afflicted with a strange condition known as tarantism, would dance frantically to the sound of music, hoping to exorcise the tarantula-like poison from their bodies. Intrigued, Alonzo began to incorporate the ritual into his performances, using his music to induce the frenzied dance. As his fame grew, so did the legend of his 'tarantella' \u2013 a mesmerizing melody that could cure the afflicted and bring the community together. Alonzo's music became synonymous with the ritual, and his name was etched in history as the 'Tarantella Maestro'.",
